Description: Local GPU-accelerated vocal/instrumental separation (Mel-Band RoFormer)
 melband-roformer is a CLI (and optional GTK4 GUI) for separating vocals
 and speech from music tracks entirely locally, using the Mel-Band
 RoFormer architecture, with NVIDIA CUDA acceleration when available and
 automatic CPU fallback otherwise. No audio is ever sent to a network
 service.
 .
 This package wraps the upstream melband-roformer-infer Python project
 (MIT licensed) and ships a self-contained Python environment (including
 PyTorch) under /usr/lib/melband-roformer/venv so it cannot conflict with
 the system Python or other Python applications. Model weights (~913 MB)
 are NOT included in this package; they are downloaded on first use with
 explicit user confirmation and sha256 verification. Requires a
 user-installed NVIDIA driver for GPU use (this package does not install
 or manage any NVIDIA kernel driver or CUDA toolkit).
 .
 Run `melband-roformer --info` or `melband-roformer --self-test` after
 installing to check your environment.
